[{:seon.task/name "a-lazy-read-records-into-the-read-it-belongs-to"
  :seon.task/plan "Root, from the owner, 2026-11-14: a missed read is a correctness bug; the cost work waits (\"Don't worry about a few ms ... We can optimize it later. Right now we dedupe and upgrade everyone\"). deps, after the fork bound. What exists: datahike.reads/with-reads binds di/*reads* to an atom while f runs, and the persistent-set index records each range it scans (di/record-read!). A lazy value made inside f and realized after f returns (an entity's attributes, a lazy seq of datoms) reads the index with *reads* unbound, so the read it belongs to never records that range, and a later change to those datoms reaches no reader. Change, in one pin, each red first: (1) a lazy read made while *reads* is bound captures the atom at its creation and records into it when realized; (2) the query planner's two direct seeks on the sorted set (query/execute.cljc:89, :215) call di/record-read! with the range each scans, and with-reads stops switching the planner off (with the planner on, those reads were silently missed: a correctness bug, agreed with root 2026-11-14). Proofs: a lazy seq of an entity's datoms realized after with-reads returns still has that entity's range in its reads; a q the planner runs records the ranges its cursors seek. Agreed with root as the one-tracker direction (root's survey, target/root/one-derivation-survey.html): every read records through di/record-read! as datom keys (function calls, config, files and pins included), and seon.profile's read set stops being a tracker; Datahike's search memo (db/search.cljc:26) and q result cache (query.cljc:2588), both keyed by the whole db's hash, are deleted once reactions hold results. See docs/storage.md#what-a-read-scanned. Held, not now: replaying ranges on a cache hit (q over 680 tasks 10 us cached vs 1,158 us recording, root's db [M])."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.db-test/a-lazy-read-records-into-the-read-it-belongs-to seon.db-test/a-planned-query-records-the-ranges-it-seeks}
  :seon.task/needs #{}} {:seon.task/name "with-reads-nests-in-an-outer-recorder"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by web-2 reviewing context's reaction core (2026-11-14) [M by reading reads.cljc:19-24]: datahike.reads/with-reads binds a fresh recorder (di/*reads*), so a read made inside a nested with-reads never reaches the outer one. Seon's reactions record every run (seon.ratom/deref-capture), so a read inside a component of a walk drawn within the render proc's pass (seon.render.proc/pass-view's d/with-reads) would be lost to the pass, and a view would not be redrawn when what only that component read moved. Today seon.ratom/deref-capture appends its reads to the outer recorder by hand (a caller patching the library). Fix in the fork: with-reads, when a recorder is bound, also records into it on return (recording composes, as Reagent's derefs compose), and the line in deref-capture goes. Proof: (with-reads #(with-reads f)) answers the inner reads in both."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{datahike.reads-test/a-nested-with-reads-records-into-the-outer}}
]
